    "title": "Baby chicks reported stolen in Randolph - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ben Breen No media credit provided. ,\n9 hours ago\nRANDOLPH, Vt. ( ABC22/FOX44 ) – Police say that even a feather of a clue would be helpful after numerous baby chicks disappeared apparently overnight from a Randolph home.\nAccording to Vermont state troopers, the chicks were last seen by their owner at the home off Vermont Route 14 on Thursday, July 9, and were discovered to be missing the next day – Friday, July 10.\nTroopers arrived Saturday to investigate; the chicks are believed to have been stolen.\nAnyone who may have information about what sort of cat burglar could be responsible for the chicks’ disappearance can call Vermont State Police, Royalton Barracks at (802) 234-9933 or submit an anonymous tip online .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ABC22 & FOX44.\n1",
    "summary": ", RANDOLPH, Vt. ( ABC22/FOX44 ) – Police say that even a feather of a clue would be helpful after numerous baby chicks disappeared apparently overnight from a Randolph home. According to Vermont state troopers, the chicks were last seen by their owner at the home off Vermont Route 14 on Thursday, July 9, and were discovered to be missing the next day – Friday, July 10. Troopers arrived Saturday to investigate; the chicks are believed to have been stolen.",
